{
 "_name": "s10_two_layer_gateway_separation",
 "_desc": "Two-layer / two-gateway cross-layer DM with the layers SEPARATED (each gateway homes on one layer and visits the other). Same lineage and commands as s09_two_layer_gateway. Joiners are STATICALLY provisioned (node_id + allowed_data_sfs) because the C++ join workstream is deferred, so no join_* emit can fire here. expect[] TRIAGED 2026-07-25 (26 -> 6): dropped as Lua-engine-only emit names with no C++ emitter (only scenarios/dv_dual_sf.lua emits them) = node_layer_info, gateway_layer_active, gateway_remote_bind_set, gateway_envelope_enqueued; dropped as never-exercised-here = join_adopted, join_data_sfs_adopted (the joiners never join). The two beacon_tx asserts were re-pointed from the retired Lua field '\"has_schedule\":true' to '\"kind\":\"gateway_window\"' - the C++ window-activation beacon (node.cpp:754), which carries the window schedule on every beacon while n_layers==2 (node_beacon.cpp:288). What is covered now: both gateways fire their window-schedule beacon + the 4 DM deliveries. KNOWN RED, DO NOT DELETE - gw_4 delivered 'l4-local-seed-to-gw': the assert is TRUE, that DM never arrives. The host resolves 'send <name>' to the target's LIVE protocolId (SimController.cpp:879) and a dual-layer gateway's id alternates with its window (gw_4 = 10 on layer 4 / 111 on layer 5), so the layer-4 send at t=70000 addressed 111 -> unroutable -> send_deferred_giveup at t=100044. The gw_5 mirror passes only because gw_5 happened to wear its home id 110 at t=78000. Delivery gate per simulation/BASELINE.md; note dm_delivery_breakdown.py drops this DM from its denominator (3/3) unless run with --all (3/4). [Carries the C++ n_layers:2/layers[] schema on its 2 gateways. ⚠ The Lua engine is DEPRECATED and UNSUPPORTED (owner ruling 2026-07-25) — run ONLY on meshroute; the historical 'run on both engines' instruction is retired.]",
